# The regression harness compares the committed baselines byte for byte and
# parses test/regress/data-manifest.txt line by line.  On Windows (MSYS2) git's
# core.autocrlf would otherwise check these files out with CRLF: every baseline
# comparison would then fail, and the manifest file names would carry a trailing
# carriage return.  Force LF in the working tree on every platform for the files
# the harness reads or compares, and for the shell scripts and Makefile that
# drive it.
test/regress/**  text eol=lf
test/regress-2000/**  text eol=lf
test/bike/**     text eol=lf
tools/*.sh       text eol=lf
*.sh             text eol=lf
Makefile         text eol=lf
